---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Legal
  title="terms of service"
  updated={site.legal.updated}
  meta={'effective · ' + site.legal.effective}
  description="the agreement between you and KomKat Studio for the loggoo app: your content stays yours, purchases are one-time, and loggoo is not health care."
>
  <p class="legal__intro">
    these terms are the agreement between you and {site.studio} for the loggoo mobile app. plain version: loggoo is a
    private daily log, your content is yours, purchases are one-time, and we ask you not to break the app or the law with it.
  </p>

  <h2>1 · who we are</h2>
  <p>
    loggoo is published by {site.studio} ("we", "us"). you can reach us any time at
    <a href={'mailto:' + site.email}>{site.email}</a>. by downloading or using loggoo you agree to these terms. if you do
    not agree, please do not use the app.
  </p>

  <h2>2 · your licence to use loggoo</h2>
  <p>
    we grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to install and use loggoo on devices you own or
    control, for your own non-commercial use. you may not copy, sell, rent, reverse-engineer, decompile or attempt to
    extract our source code, and you may not remove the loggoo watermark from generated frames in order to pass the
    output off as another product.
  </p>

  <h2>3 · no account, and what that means</h2>
  <p>
    loggoo does not require you to create an account. because there is no account, we cannot recover your moments for you
    if you lose your device, uninstall the app, or reset it without a backup. keeping cloud backup switched on, or
    exporting the frames you care about, is your safety net.
  </p>

  <h2>4 · your content</h2>
  <p>
    photos, moods, notes and frames you create in loggoo are yours. we claim no ownership of them and no licence to use
    them. they are stored on your device, and — only if you switch it on — in your own cloud storage account. you are
    responsible for having the right to photograph and store the people, places and material you log.
  </p>

  <h2>5 · acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    do not use loggoo to store or share content that is unlawful, or that infringes someone else's rights or privacy. do
    not interfere with the app's operation, attempt to bypass purchase verification, or use automated means to access
    features you have not bought.
  </p>

  <h2>6 · purchases and refunds</h2>
  <p>
    logging is free. some content — additional mood face packs and frame templates — is sold as a one-time in-app
    purchase. all payments are processed by the apple app store or google play, not by us; we never see your card
    details. purchases are tied to the store account that bought them and can be restored on that platform. refunds are
    handled under apple's or google's policies, so refund requests go to them; write to us anyway if something went wrong
    and we will help where we can.
  </p>

  <h2>7 · optional cloud sync and backup</h2>
  <p>
    if you enable backup or sync, loggoo writes a copy of your data into your own icloud or google account. that storage
    is governed by apple's or google's terms, and its availability, capacity and pricing are outside our control. we do
    not operate a loggoo server holding your photos or notes.
  </p>

  <h2>8 · changes to the app</h2>
  <p>
    we improve loggoo continuously and may add, change or retire features. if we ever have to retire a feature you paid
    for, we will say so in the release notes and offer a reasonable equivalent. we may also stop supporting older
    operating system versions.
  </p>

  <h2>9 · disclaimer — loggoo is not health care</h2>
  <p>
    loggoo helps you notice patterns in how your days feel. it is not a medical device, it does not diagnose or treat
    anything, and its trends and observations are not clinical advice. if you are struggling, please talk to a qualified
    professional or a local support line.
  </p>
  <p>
    the app is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind to the fullest extent permitted by
    law, including fitness for a particular purpose or uninterrupted operation.
  </p>

  <h2>10 · limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    to the extent permitted by law, {site.studio} is not liable for indirect, incidental or consequential damages, or for
    lost data or lost content arising from your use of loggoo. where liability cannot be excluded, it is limited to the
    amount you paid us for the app in the twelve months before the claim. nothing here limits rights you have as a
    consumer under mandatory local law.
  </p>

  <h2>11 · ending these terms</h2>
  <p>
    you may stop using loggoo and delete the app at any time. we may suspend your licence if you materially breach these
    terms — for example by attempting to circumvent purchases. sections 4, 9, 10 and 12 survive termination.
  </p>

  <h2>12 · governing law</h2>
  <p>
    these terms are governed by the laws of the jurisdiction in which {site.studio} is established, without affecting
    consumer protections that apply where you live. disputes will first be attempted to be resolved informally by email.
  </p>

  <h2>13 · updates to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    if we change these terms materially, we will update the date above and note it in the app release notes. continuing
    to use loggoo after a change means you accept the revised terms.
  </p>

  <div class="legal__contact">
    <h2>14 · contact</h2>
    <p>
      {site.studio} · <a href={'mailto:' + site.email}>{site.email}</a><br />
      we read everything that arrives and usually reply within two days.
    </p>
  </div>
</Legal>
